-- title:
--   Sections through non-strict inertia-fixed places meet the matched crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $p$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime` (that is, $p$ is a non-unit of $A$), and a package $\mathfrak X$ of type `DRModelPackage p`, which equips the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of $\mathbb Z$ in the full modular function field of level $p$ at the Igusa coordinate `IgusaScheme.jFull p` with its properness, flatness, integrality and normality data, with curve models $M_0$ over $\mathbb Q$ and $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the generic fibres together with isomorphisms $e_0$, $e_\eta$ onto the corresponding base changes and their Galois and compatibility laws, and with cusp sections, a smooth locus and the component morphisms `compInf`, `compZero`.
--
--   Two normalisations pin the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-model on the finite chart: the instance `hneη` records that the open subscheme of $M_\eta$ obtained by pulling back, along $\mathfrak X.e_\eta$ followed by `pullback.fst`, the image of the whole of the finite chart under `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin` is non-empty, and `hMη` requires that for every element $a$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull p) (IgusaScheme.jFull p)` the function on that open set induced by $a$, read in $M_\eta$'s function field and transported by $\mathfrak X.M\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ into `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, has Laurent series equal to `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series of $a$ over $\mathbb Q$.
--
--   The level bookkeeping between $1\cdot p$ and $p$ is supplied by a bijection $e_{\mathrm{Pl}}$ between the places of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` and those of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, together with `hePl_fun`: whenever $f$ at level $1\cdot p$ and $f'$ at level $p$ have the same Laurent series, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $V$ if and only if $f'$ lies in that of $e_{\mathrm{Pl}}V$, and $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f = (e_{\mathrm{Pl}}V).\mathrm{evalAt}\,f'$.
--
--   On the characteristic $p$ side: $k$ is an algebraically closed perfect field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism, `data` a `ModularPolynomialData p` satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, and `hα`, `hβ` assert the integrality of the two Hecke embeddings $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$ at level $1$ and prime $p$. Given these, $P$ is a `PlaceSpecialization A p 1 data hKr k red hα hβ` and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple P`; the hypothesis `hqN` states that $p$ does not divide $1$, and `hR` that $R$ `IsModel`, i.e. $R$ satisfies its two divisor laws and its two cusp laws at $\infty$ and $0$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces p 1 k`, the supersingular places; `hreg` and `hval` impose on $R$ the regularity law and the node value law relative to $W$ (each a conjunction of statements about residues $\mathrm{residue}_1$, $\mathrm{residue}_2$ of integral functions along node pairs, summarised here); a width function $e$ on places is given with $1 \le e\,w$ for $w \in W$ (`he`), and `hVI` imposes the value integrality law `R.ValueIntegralityLaw w` at every $w \in W$, namely that for $f$ in the node integers at $w$ and every place $V$ above $w$ under `P.reduceFst` the value $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ lies in $A$.
--
--   The inertia base is a discrete valuation ring $O$ (a commutative domain) together with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ of $O$ onto the valuation subring of the fixed field of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` obtained by pulling back $A$, with `hϖO` asserting that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$; $K$ is a fraction field of $O$, and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring homomorphism which by `hιK` carries $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,o$ to the image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $e_O(o)$ regarded inside that fixed field, which by `hιA` maps $O$ into $A$, and whose reduction is recorded by a homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa(o) = \mathrm{red}\,\langle \iota_K(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,o)\rangle$ (`htoκ`).
--
--   Over this base, $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ is a `DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O k toκ`: a regular model $Y$ over $O$ mapping properly to the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, isomorphic to it over the smooth locus and over the generic fibre, with a finite node type carrying widths, an equivalence `nodeEquiv` of nodes with the points of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$, and invertible integral component ideal sheaves. The pullback over $O$ is assumed integral (`hint`), and $\varphi$ is a ring homomorphism from its function field into `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` which is pinned on constants by `hφO` ($\varphi$ of the germ at any point of a constant $a \in O$ is the image of $\iota_K(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,a)$) and, after the non-emptiness instance `hne` for the preimage of the finite chart under `pullback.fst`, pinned on the finite chart by `hφj`: for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull p) (IgusaScheme.jFull p)` the Laurent series of $\varphi$ of the corresponding function-field element equals `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series of $a$ over $\mathbb Q$. Finally, $\sigma_N$ is a bijection from $W$ onto the nodes of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ with $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(\sigma_N w) = e\,w$ (`hσN`), and `hxj` requires for every $w \in W$ the existence of $\hat\jmath \in O$ with $\mathrm{red}\,\langle \iota_K(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\hat\jmath)\rangle = w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,1)$ and of an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk of the $O$-pullback at the image of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{nodeEquiv}(\sigma_N w)$ under `pullback.fst (𝔛.compInf k) (𝔛.compZero k)` followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, such that $\varphi(t) = \mathrm{jFun}\,1\,p - \iota_K(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\hat\jmath)$.
--
--   The conclusion is the following. Let $V$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $hw$ a proof that $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$, the specialisation under $P.\mathrm{sp}$ of the restriction of $V$ along $\bar\alpha$, lies in $W$. Assume that $V$ is fixed by the inertia group, i.e. $\mathrm{arithmeticGalois}(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(1 \cdot p))\,\sigma \cdot V = V$ for every $\sigma \in A.\mathrm{inertiaSubgroupIn}\ \mathbb Q$, and that $V$ is neither strict on the first nor on the second branch: $P.\mathrm{IsStrictFst}\,V$ fails, that is it is not the case both that the geometric Frobenius on places sends $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$ to $P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,V$ and that its square does not fix $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$; and likewise $P.\mathrm{IsStrictSnd}\,V$ fails. Then for every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} O \to$ the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$ which is a section of the structure morphism, i.e. $s$ followed by `pullback.snd` is the identity, and which extends the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point attached to $V$, in the sense that $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the composite $O \xrightarrow{e_O} A \cap \mathrm{fixedField} \hookrightarrow \mathrm{fixedField} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, followed by $s$ followed by `pullback.fst`, coincides with the morphism underlying $\mathfrak X.M\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}(e_{\mathrm{Pl}}V)$ followed by $\mathfrak X.e_\eta$ followed by `pullback.fst`, the image of the closed point of $O$ under the underlying map of $s$ is the point
--   $$\bigl(\mathrm{pullback.fst}(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k, \mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k) \ \text{followed by}\ \mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k\ \text{followed by}\ \mathrm{DRModel.baseChangeMap}\,\mathrm{to}\kappa\bigr)\bigl(\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{nodeEquiv}(\sigma_N\langle P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V, hw\rangle)\bigr),$$
--   the crossing point of the two components indexed by the node matched with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$.
--
--   This is the node-matching step in the comparison between places of the modular function field in characteristic $p$ and the crossing points of the two components of the special fibre of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model over the inertia base: an integral point whose generic point realises an inertia-fixed place that is non-strict on both branches must reduce to the crossing assigned to that place by the enumeration $\sigma_N$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts) to normalise the node enumeration in the dictionary between supersingular places and nodes.
